  "body": "Found during the work on #3460.\n\n#3460 adds the wave form of AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\": one heavy run on the trial tree of a merge wave, recorded on each PR of the wave.\n\nThe `PR-reviewer` agent (step 5) keeps the duty of #2568. When a PR has no author heavy result and no wave record on its head, the reviewer runs the reached lanes. If they cannot run, \"heavy lanes not run\" is a blocker. The test `runner_review_requires_heavy_lanes_without_author_results` pins this text.\n\nThe review comes before the planner makes a wave. Thus the reviewer runs the lanes for each PR, and the wave run saves time only for the heads that change after the review (a refresh at merge time).\n\n## Question for the maintainer\nCan a review set `merge-ready` with the heavy result \"not run - owed to the wave run before merge\"? Then the merge (not the review) waits for a green run that covers the final head. \"Not run\" stays never a pass.\n\n## Done means\n- The maintainer decides yes or no.\n- If yes: AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\", PR-reviewer step 5, the `review-prs` skill and the pinning test change together, with `Process change: yes`.\n",
